Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: support six-buffer Ethernet TX scatter/gather

QCA5332 and QCN6432 firmware API TX MSDU extension descriptors have
six 40-bit address/16-bit length buffer pairs at offset 24. Use one
linear head and up to five skb page fragments, preserving TCL bank
encapsulation and crypto by leaving the extension override clear.

Advertise SG only when all radios in the hardware group support this
layout. Linearize native Wi-Fi, unsupported fragment layouts and other
fallbacks before mutation. Keep the mapping count independent of DMA
addresses, and use the same release routine for completion and teardown.
Keep ring retries independent of DMA mapping. Report actual SG traffic
per TCL ring so a hardware benchmark can establish that it was used.

TSO remains unadvertised; one descriptor still owns one MSDU.

---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.h
@@ -134,6 +134,20 @@
 	u8 link_id;
 };
 
+#define ATH12K_TX_EXT_MAX_FRAGS 5
+
+/* Extension skbs are private to the driver, not mac80211 TX skbs. */
+struct ath12k_tx_ext_cb {
+	dma_addr_t paddr;
+	dma_addr_t frags[ATH12K_TX_EXT_MAX_FRAGS];
+};
+
+static inline struct ath12k_tx_ext_cb *ATH12K_TX_EXT_CB(struct sk_buff *skb)
+{
+	BUILD_BUG_ON(sizeof(struct ath12k_tx_ext_cb) > sizeof(skb->cb));
+	return (void *)skb->cb;
+}
